* direct bonds
* VdW 
	> atom type filter (already existed): only include C,S atoms 
	> cycle DoF filter: only include pairs that chare cycle DoFs, i.e. TorsionVec is not empty. Why? If two hydrophobic atoms are int he same rigid body subtree,
	rotating any torsion cannot hcange their distance, so they contribute only zeros to the Jacobian:
	                vdw.TorsionVec = lastCommonAncestorIdx(block_i, block_j);
                if (vdw.TorsionVec.empty()) continue; // no cycle DoFs -> skip
    > Distance filter: currently cutoffD = 0.25 
    	Change to -0.25
    > sequence separation? 
    	two hydrophobic atoms that are close in sequence (fewer than 4 residues apart) are likely connected by covalent bonds and already excluded by the rigis body model. 
    	But atoms that are neighbors in sequence but separated by rotatable bonds can still form VdW constraints. I am adding a minimum sequence separation check: 

    	// skip pairs on the same residue or adjacent residues
		if (std::abs((int)i - (int)j) < 4) continue;

