* Ideas for the future: 


> FIRST/pebble game identifies rigid clusters but provides no ranking within the rigid regions — every H-bond inside a rigid cluster is equally "important." It also gives no information about the relative motion of the flexible regions.

> KFA (Budday 2018) provides modes and a spectral gap but focuses on the V matrix (torsion space) and conformational sampling. The U matrix and per-H-bond importance ranking are not explored in that paper.

> The gap I see: Nobody has, to my knowledge, used the full SVD decomposition of the KFA Jacobian to build a weighted H-bond importance graph and connected its community structure to experimentally observable block patterns in distance-distance matrices. This would bridge rigidity analysis (topology) with spectral analysis (dynamics) in a way that produces testable predictions at the individual H-bond level


