Notes from meeting: 

On creating HBondConstrainEntity

> for the Atoms which come from the donor (that's Atom *Donor and Atom *ParentDonor) you need to be able to easily look up which subset they belong to so you can decide whether rigid body degrees of freedom apply to them or not

> so you could include AtomGroup *donorGroup and AtomGroup *acceptorGroup
inside the hbondentity

> then when you look up a row and column (I.e. DoF and Constraint) and you want to know whether that constraint is sensitive to that doF

> then you can check if the "atoms" in the DoF is equal to donorGroup (or acceptorGroup) and then you'll instantly know whether you need a non-zero value in that element

> the alternative would be to search through every atom in atoms and see if "Donor" or "Acceptor" is in there, but this would take a very long time
but instead of using HBondEntity (because you use that for other things like display in GUI) you can make an HBondConstraint which contains this information for the lookup in the Jacobian matrix

> you could in fact just reference which HBondEntity you're referring to in HBondConstraint which means you don't have to duplicate as much information
for example with an int hbond_idx which refers to the relevant HBondEntity in _hbonds


