So far: 

- Goal was: build a _dofMap that maps Jacobian row indices to DoF entries for the full protein assembly.

- What have I done: 

1. setReferenceMolecule()
	> Finds the largest connected group by atom count
	> Sets _referenceChain to that group's chain identifier
2. buildDoFMap()
	> Iterates over all connected groups (subsets)
	> For each group, finds the anchor atom's block index in the kinematic tree
	> Traverses blocks from that start index until a nullptr separator
	> Adds torsion DoF for protein chains (non-hetatm)
	> Adds 6 rigid body DoF for all non-reference groups

- Current results for crystallin: 

Chain X torsions:     1188 rows  (non-reference, also gets 6 RB DoF)
Chain X rigid body:      6 rows  OK
Chain A torsions:     1195 rows  (reference, no RB DoF) OK
Chain a waters:        438 rows  (73 waters × 6 RB DoF) OK
H1/H2/H3 extras:       18 rows  (3 × 6 RB DoF, known artefact)
