Plan for hbonds: 

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
enum ConstraintType
{
    Distance,
    AngleAlpha,
    AngleBeta,
    Dihedral1,
    Dihedral2
}


struct HBondConstraint
{
    int hbond_idx;            // index into _hbonds
    ConstraintType type;      // which of the 5 constraints
    AtomGroup *donorGroup;    // subset containing donor/hydrogen
    AtomGroup *acceptorGroup; // subset containing acceptor/parentAcceptor
    int col_idx;              // Jacobian column index
};

std::map<int, HBondConstraint> _constraintMap;  // key = Jacobian column index

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

>> Building the constraint map
For each H-bond in _hbonds, add 5 entries to _constraintMap — one per constraint type. Each entry stores which groups are affected (donor side and acceptor side).

>> Jacobian lookup
For each (row, col) pair:

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DoF &dof = _dofMap[row];
HBondConstraint &con = _constraintMap[col];

if (dof.atoms == con.donorGroup || dof.atoms == con.acceptorGroup)
{
    // compute derivative based on dof.type and con.type
}
// else: zero

>> Derivative computation

> Torsion DoF — existing gradient functions (alphaGradientHSide etc.)
> Rigid body DoF — same gradient functions with axis -> e_x/e_y/e_z and axisA -> p_c
> Reference chain — never matches any row -> naturally zero


